Remediation: To mitigate this vulnerability, replace the SHA1 hashing algorithm with stronger cryptographic hash functions, such as SHA-256 or SHA-3. These algorithms offer significantly improved security and are resistant to collision attacks, making them suitable for cryptographic purposes in modern applications.

Secure Code example:

    const crypto = require('crypto');  
    const hash = crypto.createHash('sha256').update('sensitive data').digest('hex');  
    console.log(hash);

